    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. Folding: After seeing their tiles and trumps, players can 'fold' and sit out the round to avoid penalties.\n2. The Dummy: A player can choose to play by discarding their hand and taking the 'dummy' hand.\n3. Trick Play: Lead any tile. Must follow suit. If unable to follow, you can play ANY tile (no requirement to trump unless you wish to).\n4. Winning: Highest trump wins. If no trump, highest of led suit wins.",
    Player: "1. Folding: After seeing their tiles and trumps, players can 'fold' and sit out the round to avoid penalties.\n2. The Dummy: A player can choose to play by discarding their hand and taking the 'dummy' hand.\n3. Trick Play: Lead any tile. Must follow suit. If unable to follow, you can play ANY tile (no requirement to trump unless you wish to).\n4. Winning: Highest trump wins. If no trump, highest of led suit wins.",
    objective: 'Each player starts with 15 points. Players subtract 1 point for each trick they win; if all except the dealer pass, the dealer subtracts 5 without play. A player who stays in but wins no tricks is rounced and adds 5 to their score; a player who drops out neither gains nor loses. The first to reach or pass zero points wins the game.',
    gameplay: "1. Folding: After seeing their tiles and trumps, players can 'fold' and sit out the round to avoid penalties.\n2. The Dummy: A player can choose to play by discarding their hand and taking the 'dummy' hand.\n3. Trick Play: Lead any tile. Must follow suit. If unable to follow, you can play ANY tile (no requirement to trump unless you wish to).\n4. Winning: Highest trump wins. If no trump, highest of led suit wins.",
    keyRules: [
      'Blank is the lowest rank (0), 6 is the highest (6).',
      "One end of the tile determines the 'suit', the other its rank.",
      'The winner of a trick must lead a trump next if they hold one.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
